    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7ad9b24f_ad7e63f7",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/brcm_openomci_onu/omci/brcm_uni_lock_task.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000480
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-02T04:48:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does it make any sense to use the list of UniPort instances?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 102,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 102,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "ec673fdf7dca673539600d72c9ac4b63d8d05ccd",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "196b7fdc_77aff2dc",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/brcm_openomci_onu/omci/brcm_uni_lock_task.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000436
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-02T14:18:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had considered depending on UniPort as it wraps up much of this anyway.  But when creating this task i expected at some point it could be part of the global set of tasks available in extensions/omci, given the task likely would work on all onu.  In that case i wanted it to have as few dependencies as possible on brcm adapter/handler code.\n\nChip and i have also talked about moving UniPort and other classes to the extensions/omci as well given the adtran adapter/handler classes are almost identical.",
      "parentUuid": "7ad9b24f_ad7e63f7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 102,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 102,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "ec673fdf7dca673539600d72c9ac4b63d8d05ccd",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a44193ec_e3cb1da0",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/brcm_openomci_onu/omci/brcm_uni_lock_task.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000480
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-02T14:19:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sounds good.",
      "parentUuid": "196b7fdc_77aff2dc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 102,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 102,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "ec673fdf7dca673539600d72c9ac4b63d8d05ccd",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b7d4d7bb_912be918",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/brcm_openomci_onu/omci/brcm_uni_lock_task.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000182
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-02T14:43:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would agree about moving the task into extensions/omci in the future.\n\nFor UniPort and a few others, I\u0027m leaning on creating very simple base ONU device adapter/handler that is derived from both the Adtran and BroadCom OpenOMCI ONU device adapters, perhaps in the V2.1 timeframe.  Keeping them separate may help with initial service profile implementations and after hardening, I think we would have a couple of very good examples to choose from.  This would probably be easier for an ONU adapter since the bulk of it is OMCI which is for the most part shared already.",
      "parentUuid": "a44193ec_e3cb1da0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 102,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 102,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "ec673fdf7dca673539600d72c9ac4b63d8d05ccd",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "14486326_97f0e5a1",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/brcm_openomci_onu/omci/brcm_uni_lock_task.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000480
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-02T14:46:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sounds like the beginnings of an \"openonu\" adapter (to pair with \"openolt\" adapter. Gotta like it.",
      "parentUuid": "b7d4d7bb_912be918",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 102,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 102,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "ec673fdf7dca673539600d72c9ac4b63d8d05ccd",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf788ca2_35282aa4",
        "filename": "voltha/adapters/brcm_openomci_onu/omci/brcm_uni_lock_task.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000182
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-02T14:56:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m leaning toward a base class instead of a single adapter. This would allow vendors to specialize or adopt new features for their customers (voice, CFM, DSL, ...) as needed before they get \u0027standardized\u0027 and pulled into the base classes.  May also allow a vendor to support multiple of their ONU models or code versions (patch a bug via specialized task, then revert to common code in code version with bug fix).  Of course this does not mean the base class could not be a 100% ITU compliant OMCI stack is implemented, but what are the chances of that :-)\n\nWe have a new SFU ONU coming out with which will follow this software model so that we have 3 different types of XGS-PON ONUs with a single adapter.",
      "parentUuid": "14486326_97f0e5a1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 102,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 102,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "ec673fdf7dca673539600d72c9ac4b63d8d05ccd",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
